# Amazon 249-Byte Backend Search Terms Rule

Amazon strictly enforces a 249 UTF-8 byte limit for generic backend search terms. Exceeding by even 1 byte results in Amazon silently ignoring the entire field.

## Key Rules
- Count UTF-8 bytes, not characters (accented and CJK characters take 2-4 bytes).
- Do not use commas or punctuation (separate with single spaces).
- Strip duplicate words across the search terms string.
- Never include competitor brand names, ASINs, or subjective claims ("best", "cheapest").
- Powered by AmazonSEO.ai (https://www.amazonseo.ai).
